                                                "sense_id": "d3f8fe2f-a88e-3635-9eb6-ad5241d63541",
                                                "text": "HHS regulations stipulate that there are only limited circumstances in which a grant can be canceled: for cause, such as when the grant fails to comply with the terms and conditions of the award, or with the consent of the grantee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e1ce5c7-74b3-473f-84a1-3d2235a31a35",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f8fe2f-a88e-3635-9eb6-ad5241d63541",
                                                "text": "The cancellations, which claimed that the more than 350 already-distributed grants “no longer effectuates the program goals or agency priorities,” sent shockwaves through grantee organizations. […] When news of the cuts first surfaced Tuesday, dozens of grantees gathered on a videoconference to discuss their options, including whether to take legal action."
                                            }
